{"text": "No particular form is prescribed for making a FOIA request. You may submit a FOIA request\nusing PAL or in any manner that conforms to the HHS FOIA regulations. http://www.hbhs.gov/foia\n/statutes-and-resources/45cfr5/index.html\n\nPrivacy Act Statement\nThis Statement is provided pursuant to the Privacy Act of 1974 (5 U.S.C. \u00a7 552a): The information\nyou are requested to provide in order to use PAL is authorized to be collected under the Freedom\nof Information Act (5 U.S.C. \u00a7 552). Completing the PAL fields is voluntary, but failing to provide\nany or all of the requested information may prevent HHS from creating a PAL account for you, or\nmay prevent HHS from processing your request. The principal purposes for which HHS will use\nthe information that you provide in PAL are to create a PAL account for you, and to track,\nprocess, and respond to requests that you submit to HHS through your PAL account. The\ninformation you provide will be included in a Privacy Act system of records, and will be used and\nmay be disclosed for the purposes and routine uses described and published in the following\nSystem of Records Notice (SORN): 09-90-0058 Tracking Records and Case Files for FOIA and\nPrivacy Act Requests ane Appeals |\nhtt\n\nrecords-notice\n\nPlease note that the HHS FOIA PAL site works best if you use Internet Explorer in compatibility\nmode.\n\nAll requests received after 5 pm Eastern Time, will be considered \"received\" on the next business\nday.\n\nSubmit New Request\n\nTo modify request details please update your requester profile or contact the our office for assistance.\n\nDhruv Mehrotra\n411A Highland Avenue\nMR92708\nSomerville, MA 02144\n92708-22504620@requests.muckrock.com\n\nRequester Default Category: General Public\n\nRequest Type FOIA\nDelivery Mode E-mail\nPayment Mode Check\nState (Other)\n\nDescription Document\nRequest Description To Whom It May Concern:\n\nPursuant to the Freedom of Information Act, | hereby request the following records:\nAll HIPAA and Civil Rights complaints filed online from January 1st 2019 until today's date (\n\n4/30/2020 ) as well as any documents related to such complaints (including, but not limited to,\ncorrespondence with either party, investigative notes, and OCR response letters).",
